==Trivia==
* For some reason, due to high ping, a glitch may happen involving the [X] move staying on top of the Yeti's transformations head and staying there.
* Multiple of Yeti's skills have had their name changed after the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NwOlsLgAC0I Yeti Fruit Showcase] video.
** Those being, '''Ice Clap''' to '''Arctic Clap''', '''Glacial Toss''' to '''Frostbite Boulder''', '''Afterimage Assault''' (Which Most Likely WAS a mistake) to '''Glacial Execution''' and '''Arctic Tackle''' to '''Tundra Rush'''.
** The {{Ability|Z}}, is very similar to unawakened [[Magma]]'s {{Ability|Magma|Z}}, which is further reinforced by the fact that {{Ability|Z}}'s original name was '''[Z] Ice Clap'''. Moreover, Yeti's transformed {{Ability|C}} move is somewhat akin to Magma's awakened {{Ability|Magma|X|2}} move, in that both moves are basically harnessing their respective elements into their fist and then blasting the foe away with tremendous forces.
** Additionally, the old [C] move '''(Afterimage Assault)''' had the same skill name as [[Tiger]]'s {{Ability|Tiger|C}} move, meaning that the fruit was likely copy-pasted as a placeholder from Tiger when it was in development.
** The two following statements above heavily reinforce the fact that Yeti might have been a rushed fruit for the winter Christmas update in 2024.
* Yeti's {{Ability|C}} rotates the camera best if the user has shift-lock enabled, making it quite annoying for people who don't usually play Shift-lock because sometimes it doesn't rotate. If the player teleports on water, it will create an ice platform for them. This platform lasts longer than the Frost Walker ability, similar to the {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|X}}.
* Yeti and [[Tiger]] used to be the third pair of fruits to share the same price, the second being [[Gas]] and [[Control]], and the first being [[Mammoth]] and [[T-Rex]], however they are now the second pair as of [[Updates/29.0|Update 29]].
* Yeti is the second [[Beast]]-type fruit that allows its user to walk on [[water]], with the first being [[Kitsune]]. (Since Awakened [[Buddha]] doesn't actually walk on water). In addition, it is also the third fruit in the game, as of [[Update 25]], to create its perspective elemental platforms, being ice, similar to the fruit with the same name and [[Magma]].
* The player will teleport to the other side of a wall if they use {{Ability|C}} on an [[Enemies|enemy]] that is behind a wall/obstacle. This is only the case when the user has shift-lock enabled.
* Yeti also shares the same name with the [[Yeti (Boss)|Yeti (boss)]] from the [[First Sea]]'s [[Frozen Village]].
* Yeti with [[Pilot Helmet]] while dashing moves at the same speed as the [[Beast Hunter]].
* Yeti serves as an effective counter to hybrid and untransformed [[Dragon]] users, due to the incredibly low cooldown of its moves.
* Yeti is good against [[Buddha]] users as the high knockback can push them away rendering their M1 useless.
* Yeti is the first and currently the only fruit in the game to start with the letter 'Y'.
* Yeti is considered as one of the best fruits for [[Sea Events]] alongside [[Magma]], [[Gas]], [[Phoenix]], [[Blizzard]], [[Mammoth]] and [[Dragon]], since all of the attacks can damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Depending on where the user is positioned, {{Ability|X}} can have infinite range, as the projectile's premise is just like a catapult boulder.
* {{Ability|X}} can be held for only 30 seconds.
* {{Ability|C}} (when hit) actually ''has'' [[Destructible Physics]]. The weird part is that only the ''untransformed'' version has Destructible Physics, while the transformed version does not.
* The ice platforms last for a different amount of time depending on their size and on the move the player used to create them. The smallest ice platform (Untransformed {{Ability|C}}) lasts for around 8 seconds, while the biggest ice platform (Transformed {{Ability|X}}) lasts for around 58 seconds.
* Yeti can be really good against [[Rumbling Waters]] as the user only needs to spam their M1's at the center of the Rumbling Waters to hit all three [[Sea Beast]]s. It is also very good against [[Piranha]]s when they sneak up from behind as this fruit is quick with [[Area of Effect|AoE]] attacks that can push them away. On top of that, it can create ice platforms, allowing teammates to stay above the water even without the [[Shark]] race.
** Other players can step on the ice passively created by the Yeti user's feet, thus being able to continuously follow a Yeti user while staying above the water. This can be useful as the Yeti can help others travel across the ocean without needing a boat.
* {{Ability|Yeti|C}}'s aerial variant shares a similar sound effect to [[Dragonstorm]]'s {{Ability|Dragonstorm|X}}.
* Before Yeti's nerf in [[Updates/26|Update 26]], Yeti was one of the most commonly used fruits in [[PvP mechanics|PvP]] due to its heavy spamming abilities.
* Yeti transformation is recommended in any situation over the untransformed version due to its higher damage output, lesser knockback and shorter cooldowns.
* Yeti was released during the [[Christmas Event|Christmas event]] where [[Presents]] are given out, fitting for it's icy theme.
* Yeti's transformed moves are highly chainable even as a "spam fruit", which sets it apart from other "spam fruits" e.g [[Kitsune]]. This is partly why this fruit was extremely powerful before it was nerfed.
* Yeti is extremely good in [[PvP mechanics|PvP]] when in water due to the ice platforms it makes. This allows the user to put pressure on the enemy because the enemy has to worry about drowning and being hit at the same time, often overwhelming.
* Yeti and [[Buddha]] are the only [[Beast]] fruits representing a partial human, with [[Buddha]] representing {{w|Budai}} and Yeti representing a Snow-like ape or "Wild human".
* Yeti's Transformation has somewhat similar clothes to [[Tiger]], as they both wear clothing on their legs with a mainly dark hue.

* There is a visual bug/change where the frosty aura around the transformed Yeti will only appear when the untransformed {{Ability|V}}, transformed dash, {{Ability|C}} and {{Ability|F}} are activated, but it will only last for a few seconds before dissipating. The frosty aura around the Yeti's mouth remains the same.
* There is a bug where if the user has high ping and uses transformed {{Ability|X}}, the ice ball will stay over the Yeti and will stay until eventually using the move again. The same thing happens if the user gets stunned while casting the move, except it disappears shortly after.
** This can also happen in the base (untransformed) form, except this time the snowball will be stuck to the user's right arm.
* There is a glitch that the user does not have a frosty mist around them when transformed, and it's purely client side only. For some reason, there are players that experience the missing frosty mist only on their account and not other people, which lead to the images of the Yeti transformed on this page being much clearer and neater without the mist.
** It could be a matter of the texture breaking after frequent usage, as this problem does not arise when the player transforms for the first time.
*[[Tiger]] is considered the rival of this fruit as they were shown fighting in their respective rework/release trailers, and both Yeti and [[Tiger]] stand as the pinnacle of non-fury-meter [[Beast]] fruits.
* There is currently a visual bug/glitch where when the user Flash Steps while transformed, the ice clone appears where the player Flash Stepped onto.
* There is a glitch that when using {{Ability|F}} in the air there is a chance that the user will get teleported under the map.
* Yeti and [[Love]]'s "Lovestruck" effect still shake the screen even with Camera Shake off.
* [[Fiend]]'s sound effect when walking on [[water]] (Fiend's Cursed Strider passive) is the exact same sound effect as Yeti when walking on water (Yeti's Frost Walker passive) even though Fiend's Cursed Strider passive is not ice.
* A [[Mutations|mutation]] for Yeti was teased in [[The Blox Bulletin|The Blox Bulletin #19]].
** Said mutation, being [[Fiend]].

